 both old and new  have probably never heard of this  obscure character who first appeared in  fantastic four  issue 353 in 1991. mr mobius is in  charge of prosecuting the fantastic four  for their time travelling shenanigans  that tracks with what we see in the  trailer there's a high-tech looking film  strip  that seems to be evident against loki  then mobius sitting at a table with loki  who's clearly being held prisoner by the  tva  mr mobia seems to be taking loki to task  for his crimes against time  and possibly putting him to work to set  some things right  three very ominous looking figures loom  large in the offices of the tva  first they show up as three giant heads  hanging behind gugu on batara  who's playing an as yet unnamed  character we see them again as three  gigantic statues  who are they as ever the pages of marvel  comics hold the most probable answer  these are most likely the time keepers  characters whose origins are tied to the  time variance authority  their story is very very complicated and  involves multiple timelines in perfect  past versions of themselves called the  time twisters and a guy named  zarko the tomorrow man whether we'll see  or hear more of them or just see the  statues in the background isn't known at  this point  in a blink and you'll miss it moment a  group of tva agents  along with loki march into a big box  store called roxcut  that name bears a striking similarity to  one of the many fictional corporations  that have shown up in marvel comics over  the years  roxanne energy corporation if you've  played through 2020 spider-man miles  morales video game  you're already familiar with roxanne and  his nefarious corporate misdeeds roxanne  has been in the mcu from the start  with their logo appearing on a building  during the climactic fight in iron man  the president even says the name in iron  man 3.  this is the roxanne norco roxanne has  also been a key part of several  mcu tv shows and the logo is on a gas  pump 